# Monitor: DEBUG shm mirror

## Scope

- **DEBUG builds only** (`--enable-debug`); release uses inline no-ops in `stats_buffer_debug_shm.h`.
- Mirrors latest full payloads under `HPCPERFSTATS_DEBUG_SHM_DIR` (default `/dev/shm/hpcperfstatsd-debug`):
  - **`schema`** — complete `$` rotation payload (`write_hdr=1`)
  - **`fast`** — latest `@fast` sample (single payload)
  - **`full`** — latest `@full` (or legacy full-width) sample (single payload)
  - **`fast.burst` / `full.burst`** — all payloads from the latest sample tick
    (shared-node: every jid + node-wide `-`), parts separated by `#---burst-part---`
  - **`sentinels`** — one line per key not OK this cycle: `type dev key code slug errno site first last count` (provenance from `src/stats_sentinel_debug.c`)
  - **`sentinel_sites`** — every registered `stats_set_missing*` call site with its hit count (the live coverage source for `FAULT_INJECT`; **monitor-value-sentinel-contract**)
- **Shared-node multi-jid:** `job_shared_emit` must not mirror the trailing
  node-wide `-` insert into `fast`/`full` (it would hide the last jid sample).
  Idle `-` (zero discovered jids) still mirrors. Burst files always include every
  insert from the tick (`burst_begin` / `burst_append` / `burst_commit`).

## Implementation

- **Permissions**: directory `0700`, files `0600` (payloads contain jobid, host, metrics).
- **Dir resilience**: each write calls `stats_buffer_debug_shm_ensure_dir()` → `ensure_private_dir` so a mid-run `rm -rf` of the mirror dir is recreated on the next sample/schema write — daemon does not abort; reject non-owned / group-writable dirs.
- **Atomic write**: `O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW` tmp + `rename`; log failures via `monitor_log_debug` (do not `(void)` discard).
- **Env**: copy `HPCPERFSTATS_DEBUG_SHM_DIR` into owned storage — do not retain `getenv()` pointer; allow only absolute paths under `/dev/shm/` without `..`.
- **Gating**:
  - `stats_buffer_debug_shm_schema_wanted(write_hdr, payload_ok)` → schema file when `write_hdr && payload_ok`
  - `stats_buffer_debug_shm_sample_wanted(write_hdr, payload_ok)` → sample files when `!write_hdr && payload_ok`
- **Write API**: `stats_buffer_debug_shm_write_payload(sf, kind)` with `STATS_BUFFER_DEBUG_SHM_PAYLOAD_{SCHEMA,FAST,FULL}`.

## Tests

- Unit + golden: `tests/test_stats_buffer_debug_shm.c`, `test_debug_shm_emit_*`, `test_debug_shm_schema_mirror.c`.
- Assert gating helpers match `monitor_daemon_collect_to_ring` behavior.
- Slug-named goldens: `tests/expected/shm_{schema,fast,full}_<capability_slug>.txt` (**monitor-shm-message-correctness**).
- Document the DEBUG requirement in **`monitor/docs/reference/source-modules.md`** (DEBUG mirror section; **monitor-readme-maintenance**).

